  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing Dialogues, Solidarity, and Accountability for SRHR in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the 30th anniversary of the Beijing Platform for Action approaches, this project aims to build a diverse, intersectional network of women&#x2019;s rights activists and civil society organizations to advance Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) in the Philippines. By bringing together key stakeholders&#x2014;including women&#x2019;s rights groups and state actors&#x2014;the initiative seeks to amplify advocacy through collaborative discussions, storytelling, and campaigns, all inspired by the Beijing Platform&#x2019;s goals. 

The initiative includes three core components led by Likhaan Center for Women&#x2019;s Health, Filipino Freethinkers (FF), and the Women&#x2019;s Global Network for Reproductive Rights (WGNRR). Likhaan will convene women&#x2019;s rights organizations (WROs) to identify and advocate for the rights needs of women and marginalized groups. FF will use creative storytelling to shift SRHR narratives, while WGNRR will strengthen SRHR networks and facilitate collaborative campaigns. Together, these efforts will</narrative>
  </description>
